Version 4.10, December 23, 2014

No changes.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 4.9, April 17, 2014

No changes.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 4.8, October 18, 2013

7/19/13  [EDGcpfe/10662]
C++11 const-correctness

C++11 removed the previously-deprecated implicit conversion from a narrow
string literal to char*.  In order to permit their compilation as C++11
code, edgcc.c and pl_nm.c have been changed to use the new a_const_char
typedef that has been added to basics.h (see the EDGcpfe/10662 entry in
the src/Changes file for a more detailed discussion).


7/19/13  Fix warnings in edgcc.c compilation with EDG front end

A number of warnings were issued when edgcc.c was compiled with our front
end (some of which only occurred on non-Windows system, which is really
only intended for testing purposes).  Now fixed.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 4.2

8/25/10  Handle object files with large numbers of symbols in pl_nm

The pl_nm command is invoked by edg_prelink to display symbols from
object files in a format acceptable to the prelinker.  pl_nm did not
work properly for certain object files with a very large number of
symbols.  Now fixed.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 4.0

12/8/08  Avoid linker warnings on default libraries

When EDG_MSCV_VERSION is >= 1300 the /NODEFAULTLIB:LIBC option is now
passed to the linker to suppress warnings that can occur when edgcc is used
on a different version of Windows from the one on which it was built.

12/8/08  Use /Fe option instead of -o to name executable

The -o option has been deprecated by Microsoft, so edgcc now uses the /Fe
option is used instead.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 3.1

6/12/02  Add EDG_PRELINK_DEFAULT_OPTIONS

The environment variable EDG_PRELINK_DEFAULT_OPTIONS may now be used to
specify options to be used when invoking the prelinker.

5/23/02  Support for Microsoft C version 7

edgcc has been updated to work with the version 7 tools.  The version
7 linker no longer includes symbol information in the .exe file, so
edg_munch cannot be used.  An improved static initialization mechanism
is now used the eliminates the need for edg_munch.

edg_munch is still needed when targeting older versions of the Microsoft
compiler.  A new environment variable named EDG_MSVC_VERSION can be
used to specify that an older version is being used.  It should be
set to 1200 if MSVC version 6 is being used.
